# =====================================================================
# kernel.clausal -- the SHARED FLOOR for eu/procurement/framework_agreements (constraint-satisfaction family).
# DAG root of the determination-slices layout. It holds ONLY what more than
# one file needs: the result CONSTRUCTORS, the pinned verdict vocabulary,
# and the profile KEY atoms / checklist row ids shared across the slices.
# Atoms + constructors ONLY -- no rules, no facts.
#
# Source: Directive 2014/24/EU Art 33 (OJ L 94, 28.3.2014).
#
# NOTHING SINGLE-CONSUMER LIVES HERE. A name only ONE file spells is
# declared in THAT file -- its `-module(...)` list when a result or a
# sibling exposes it, `-private([...])` otherwise. Promote a name to this
# file the moment a SECOND file needs it, and only then.
#
# Declaring an atom mints a MODULE-LOCAL identity: two files declaring the
# same name mint two classes that never unify, and the failure is SILENT.
# So every bare atom has exactly ONE declaring file in this package and
# every other user imports it from that owner.
# =====================================================================
-module(kernel, [
    # result constructors -- one per determination
    framework_term_verdict(STATUS, DEFECT_IDS, CITATIONS),
    call_off_verdict(STATUS, ROUTE, DEFECT_IDS, CITATIONS),
    framework_agreements_verdict(STATUS, CITATIONS),

    # placeholder vocabulary retained for scaffold compatibility (ADDITIVE-VOCABULARY RULE)
    satisfied,
    not_satisfied,
    overall,
    as_of_date
])
-double_quotes(chars)
